      <rules>
        <rule name="Pikes" id="5704-eb2d-b360-b499" hidden="false">
          <description>A warrior equipped with a pike can support an allied figure in contact with an enemy in the same way as a spearman. It can also support an allied figure through another supporting figure in a straight line. To do so, the pikeman must be in contact with the figure supporting the engaged model in such a way that a straight line can be traced between the centre of its base, the support’s base, and the engaged ally’s base.

A pike inflicts a -1 penalty to the enemy’s defence rolls.


Watch out though, because pikes are unwieldy weapons. A pike also inflicts a -1 penalty to its bearer’s defence rolls against both melee and shooting attacks.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Mercenaries" id="de3f-4794-cae0-a0f3" hidden="false">
          <description>50% of your Byzantine army can be composed of warriors or special characters recruited from other armies.

Your chieftain must always be Byzantine.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Composite Bows" id="6b65-2a3c-b62b-8bd3" hidden="false">
          <description>Byzantine warriors don’t have access to bows, only composite bows. These have the same characteristics as bows, except that their range is 30”</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Mounted Archers" id="08cb-66e7-31f2-bcbd" hidden="false">
          <description>Byzantine cavalry can be equipped with composite bows.


Their use imposes the same restrictions on cavalry as on infantry</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="min" value="50" field="4163-7d26-88e5-be23" scope="roster" shared="true" id="6c42-2ee7-71f8-75e0" percentValue="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="true"/>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="forces" scope="roster" shared="true" id="8760-19ef-ec38-7259-min" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="true"/>
